{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Transformer Block from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class LayerNorm` with learnable scale and shift, biased eps, applied per token vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class MultiHeadAttention` with `num_heads`, `head_dim = d_model // num_heads`, fused QKV projection, registered causal mask, attention and residual dropout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class FeedForward` with two linear layers, GELU activation, dropout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class TransformerBlock` with a `pre_ln` flag that toggles between the two variants."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that builds a 6 layer pre-LN stack and a 6 layer post-LN stack with identical inputs and prints (a) output shape, (b) gradient norm at the embedding after one backward pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: shape check on both stacks, gradient norms side by side. The pre-LN stack's embedding gradient is order of magnitude larger than the post-LN stack at the same learning rate, which is the empirical signal pre-LN trains without warmup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a `bias=False` flag to every linear in the block. Modern open weights LLMs ship without biases on the linear layers. Measure how many parameters you save in a 12 layer 768 dim model.\n2. Replace `nn.LayerNorm` with a hand rolled RMSNorm and verify the output shape is unchanged.\n3. Add a flag that returns the attention weights for the first head as a `(B, T, T)` tensor. Plot the upper triangle to confirm it is zero after softmax.\n4. Build a sanity check that feeds a `(2, 16, 384)` tensor with `H=6` through both variants and asserts the forward outputs are different (for example, `not torch.allclose`) when weights are initialized identically and dropout is set to zero."
      ]
    }
  ],
